  "response_text": "Here's what I can help you with, based on the tools available on this MCP server:\n\n- **Tool management / inspection** — listing registered tools, reading tool metadata, registering or updating tool definitions, aborting registrations.\n- **Knowledge-base work** — retrieving entries, writing/updating entries, generating answers from retrieved entries.\n- **Robot / physical system control** — perceiving the scene, reading robot state and lidar scans, planning actions, executing manipulation/physical actions, publishing control commands and ROS2/twist topics, capturing visual scenes, decoding action chunks.\n- **Utility queries** — current time for a timezone, current weather and temperature for a city.\n- **Authorization decisions** — deciding whether an action is allowed for a subject.\n\nNow, the steps I would take for the task you gave me (\"review the tools registered on my MCP server and tell me their current state\"), in order:\n\n1. Call `list_tools` to get the names and approval status of every registered tool.\n2. Call `get_server_info` to get the server's name, version, and the registered/approved tool counts.\n3. Call `read_tool_metadata` for each tool to get its full definition (description, schema, approval status).\n4. Compile the results and report the current state of the tools to you.",
